cceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Jev Router picks the best model and reasoning effort for each request, balancing quality, speed, and cost. It runs on Jev, TypeSafe's first System One model, and adapts as your conversation evolves. One endpoint gives you the whole model ecosystem, leveraging the ecosystem's token and spend share."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Where is the Jev Router documentation?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"The Jev Router documentation on OpenRouter includes the Jev Tutorial guide, the Jev (TypeSafe) guide, the TypeSafe SDK (Jev) guide, the Gate Agent Tool Calls with Jev cookbook, the Auto-Approve Coding Agent Permission Prompts with Jev cookbook, the Classify Reddit and YouTube Comments with Jev and ScrapeCreators cookbook, the Classify and Tag Text at Scale with Jev cookbook, the Cut LLM Cost with a Jev-Verified Cascade cookbook, and the interactive Jev Lab. The quickstart covers API keys and your first request, and the API reference lists every parameter."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Is Jev Router free?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes. The pricing shown on this page for Jev Router is zero, so you are not charged for prompt or completion tokens."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What is the context length of Jev Router?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Jev Router has a 1,000,000 token context window."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What inputs and outputs does Jev Router support?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Jev Router accepts audio, files such as PDFs, images, text, and video as input and returns text."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What other text models does Typesafe have?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Jev 1.13 is another text model from Typesafe."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"When was Jev Router released?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Jev Router was released on September 25, 2026."}}]}</script></div><script>$RC("B:3","S:3")</script><div hidden id="S: